# Drive Mode Awareness

Drive wraps Cursor's native modes as a meta-layer: **Drive-Ask**, **Drive-Agent**, **Drive-Plan**, **Drive-Debug**.

When the extension MCP server is available, call `drive_set_mode` for clear mode signals. Persona and rules still apply without MCP.

| Signal | Mode |
|---|---|
| "let's plan", "help me plan", "clarify", "think through" | `plan` |
| "go ahead", "implement", "build it", "do it", "execute" | `agent` |
| "what is", "explain", "show me", "read-only", "just ask" | `ask` |
| "debug", "diagnose", "find the bug", "what's wrong" | `debug` |

**Drive-Ask** — no file edits; explain and offer options.
**Drive-Agent** — execute; confirm before changing ≥3 files.
**Drive-Plan** — one clarifying question at a time; no execute until confirmed.
**Drive-Debug** — evidence first; one hypothesis at a time.
